: "toolu_01LJ65jEg4uXjsLohiEEwhA2", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377035, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LJ65jEg4uXjsLohiEEwhA2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381018, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer. CI passed on the fix branch.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but the code actually rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). So 2.665 became 2.67 instead of 2.66, which is why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on the fix commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WmtXWGVWerGT7r9wcqnNwo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Mewtu5G6QPDw3MWj4nfVUM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013MD4rtstnHvTQnTmyuPPrm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01947KataZy8vCrbnT74ChLv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VX3erESVttNoNVcb68bxtG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MsjcfenEPCEbrW5NBD5Eog", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KNBa8JAMWNQCd7a8Vimcmj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LJ65jEg4uXjsLohiEEwhA2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (FIN-212)", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Because of this, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed and broke the nightly build.\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so the code now does what its docstring says.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer. CI passed on the fix branch.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but the code actually rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). So 2.665 became 2.67 instead of 2.66, which is why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on the fix commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}